title: Tasks
kind: overview
aliases: task
summary: Long daemon work — a reconcile, a duplicate scan, a flush — runs as a task any client can observe, follow and often stop.

Some daemon work can take a long time on a large repository: a full reconcile, a
duplicate scan, a watcher flush carrying a whole directory tree, a slow query.
The daemon runs each as a ''task'': an observable unit of work with a progress
record that any client can poll — a bar when the amount of work is known, a
spinner otherwise.

A task is not tied to the request that started it: closing the GUI or the command
line mid-reconcile does not interrupt it, and a client that comes back resumes
observing it. (The word ''task'' is used because the event log already calls its
rows ''operations''.)

